# Lane stages

Every lane thread reports in four stages, one line each, in this exact form, as the last line of the report:

- `Scope · <what the lane will do> · doc <url>` once the scope doc is published with `plan-publish --scope`. Build nothing until Alex approves.
- `Working · <what moved> · <next step or blocker>` at each milestone.
- `Review · <proof on prod> · Accept or send back` when the work is landed and proved.
- `Done · accepted <ET time>` after Alex accepts.

Finishing a lane is the lane's own job: run `lane-close <lane>`, end with the Done line, then settle your own thread with T3's thread tool (`t3_thread_organize`, action `settle`, no threadId; it applies when the turn ends). No coordinator or person settles it; the thread-watcher only reminds a Done thread that is still open.

No priority tags in thread titles; pin is the only ordering (Alex, 2026-10-27, F5 scope).
